OL,3,COutbreak of Bluetongue threatens
OL,4,Clivestock
OL,6,FMore than three-quarters of
OL,7,F'Bluetongue' cases across England are
OL,8,Fbeing reported in the West Country.
OL,10,FThe disease, which mainly impacts
OL,11,Fsheep and cattle, is spread by midges.
OL,12,FIt does not pose a risk to humans.
OL,14,FHow many cases have there been?
OL,16,FIn July, 81 cases were reported across
OL,17,FEngland and 69 of those were in the
OL,18,FSouth West - including 39 in Devon, 20
OL,19,Fin Somerset and nine in Cornwall.
OL,21,F'Heartbreaking'
OL,1,W~s1j5 hw1~k4~c1 hw}h7}j7}      G1/6
